  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{8}{{x}^{5}},\\, & x\\ge 1, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven the function $f(x)$ above, which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\ge 1$\n- ${\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n- $f(x)$ is a valid probability density function",
  "worked_solution": "For a function $f(x)$ to be a valid probability density function on a set $S,$ it must satisfy the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\in S$\n\n- ${\\int }_{S}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n\nNow, let's consider each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, for $x\\ge 1,$ we have $f(x)=\\frac{8}{{x}^{5}}\\ge 0.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Indeed,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{8}{{x}^{5}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{{x}^{4}}\\,{|}_{1}^{\\infty } \\\\  & =-(0-2) \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since statement II is false, $f(x)$ is not a valid probability density function.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"",
